{# Session R2-BUILD. Placed here deliberately: the hypothesis list sits between
   the evidence this reading produced and the measurements recommended next, so
   an analyst reads "what was found" -> "what could have caused it" -> "what to
   collect to tell them apart" in that order.

   The {% if %} wrapper is not redundant with the macro's own guard. `{{ ... }}`
   is an expression, not a block tag, so trim_blocks does NOT eat the newline
   after it -- calling the macro unconditionally left one blank line behind in
   every report with no bearing fault. A block tag IS eaten, so wrapping the
   call makes a report without a cause section byte-identical to the
   pre-R2-BUILD one. #}
